-- title:
--   Dwork-type lifting of a power series to ghost components
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring and $p$ a prime such that $p\cdot 1$ is a non-zero-divisor in $\mathcal O$ and $c^p-c$ lies in the ideal $(p)$ for every $c\in\mathcal O$. Let $\tau$ be a finite type of variables, let $M$ be a natural number, and let $H$ be a multivariate formal power series in $\mathcal O[[X_\tau]]$ (indices being finitely supported functions $\mu:\tau\to\mathbb N$) subject to the hypothesis that for every index $\mu$ and every variable $t\in\tau$ the product $\mu(t)\cdot \mathrm{coeff}_\mu(H)$, with $\mu(t)$ taken as an element of $\mathcal O$ via the natural cast, lies in the ideal generated by $p^{M-1}$ (natural subtraction, so the exponent is $0$ when $M=0$). The conclusion asserts the existence of a Witt vector $\ell\in W(\mathcal O[[X_\tau]])$ (Witt vectors for the prime $p$ over the power series ring) whose first $M$ ghost components are the $p$-power substitution untwists of $H$: for every $n<M$ and every index $\mu'$, the $\mu'$-coefficient of the $n$-th ghost component of $\ell$ equals the coefficient of $H$ at the index $p^{M-1-n}\mu'$. In particular the $(M-1)$-st ghost component of $\ell$ is $H$ itself. No uniqueness is claimed.
--
--   This is the power series form of Dwork's lemma: a family of candidate ghost components is realised by an actual Witt vector once consecutive members satisfy the Frobenius congruences, here for the lift of Frobenius given by the substitution $X_t\mapsto X_t^p$. It is the engine used to produce the logarithm covectors of a multivariate formal group, and is cited by the results on the coefficients of such covectors ([`MvFormalGroup.coeff_map_subst_sub_map_sub_map_mem_of_forall_coeff_ghostComponent_eq_logCovector`](thm.html#MvFormalGroup.coeff_map_subst_sub_map_sub_map_mem_of_forall_coeff_ghostComponent_eq_logCovector), [`MvFormalGroup.coeff_mem_span_sup_pow_of_forall_coeff_ghostComponent_eq_logCovector_of_slope`](thm.html#MvFormalGroup.coeff_mem_span_sup_pow_of_forall_coeff_ghostComponent_eq_logCovector_of_slope) and [`MvFormalGroup.coeff_sub_coeff_mem_of_forall_coeff_ghostComponent_eq_logCovector_of_le`](thm.html#MvFormalGroup.coeff_sub_coeff_mem_of_forall_coeff_ghostComponent_eq_logCovector_of_le)).
